  "snippet": "Release: datasette-maplibre 0.1a0 The first new Datasette geospatial plugin in quite a while! This one combines the excellent MapLibre GL library with OpenFreeMap, the free vector map server operated by Zsolt Ero (you sh...",
  "coverImage": "https://static.simonwillison.net/static/cors-allow/2026/datasette-maplibre.webp",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-maplibre/releases/tag/0.1a0\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-maplibre 0.1a0</a></p>\n<p>The first new Datasette geospatial plugin in quite a while! This one combines the excellent <a href=\"https://maplibre.org/maplibre-gl-js/docs/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">MapLibre GL</a> library with <a href=\"https://openfreemap.org\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">OpenFreeMap</a>, the free vector map server operated by Zsolt Ero (you should <a href=\"https://github.com/sponsors/hyperknot\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">sponsor Zsolt on GitHub</a>.)</p>\n<p>I built most of this with a single prompt to Claude Fable 5.2:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>Look at datasette-cluster-map and datasette-leaflet-geojson plugins, then look at ~/dev/tools/openfreemap-demo.html - then build a brand new Datasette plugin that uses maplibreGL and openfreemap and combines the features of those other two plugins - but be creative and think outside the box for other useful features the plugin might have</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>\"Be creative and think outside the box\" resulted in a few neat ideas - my favorite is that it displays SVG previews of GeoJSON shapes, then loads a WebGL preview only when they scroll into view.</p>\n<p>I also had Claude build a comprehensive demo which works in the latest Datasette Lite, so you can <a href=\"https://lite.datasette.io/?install=datasette-maplibre&amp;url=https://gist.githubusercontent.com/simonw/39fa5d399465766039549912e2b3d291/raw/f6dfba99a75cbb8b5d9386223220eb52272767ee/demo.db&amp;metadata=https://gist.githubusercontent.com/simonw/39fa5d399465766039549912e2b3d291/raw/f6dfba99a75cbb8b5d9386223220eb52272767ee/metadata.yml\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">visit this link</a> to load the plugin and a demo database in your browser via Pyodide and WebAssembly.</p>\n<p>I like <a href=\"https://lite.datasette.io/?install=datasette-maplibre&amp;url=https://gist.githubusercontent.com/simonw/39fa5d399465766039549912e2b3d291/raw/f6dfba99a75cbb8b5d9386223220eb52272767ee/demo.db&amp;metadata=https://gist.githubusercontent.com/simonw/39fa5d399465766039549912e2b3d291/raw/f6dfba99a75cbb8b5d9386223220eb52272767ee/metadata.yml#/demo/capitals_and_countries%23map=0/4.2/180&amp;color=continent\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">this demo page</a> showing both GeoJSON shapes and lat/lon points on the same map:</p>\n<p><img alt='Screenshot of a web map interface. Toolbar: \"View\" set to \"Clusters\", \"Colour by\" set to \"continent\", plus \"Filter to this area\" and \"Download GeoJSON\" buttons. A world map shows countries outlined and shaded by continent, with coloured dots and numbered cluster circles. A popup for a point in South America reads: capital Caracas, country Venezuela, continent South America, capital_population 2985000, latitude 10.502944, longitude -66.918983. Legend: Africa (52), Asia (45), Europe (39), North America (16), South America (13), Oceania (6). Text: \"All 171 rows are on the map\". Below, a table with columns country, continent, capital_population, latitude, longitude, boundary. First row: Afghanistan, Asia, 3277000, 34.518636, 69.181314, with a small map in the boundary column showing Afghanistan outlined and shaded in blue.' loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/cors-allow/2026/datasette-maplibre.webp\"/></p>\n<p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/visualization\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">visualization</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/generative-ai\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">generative-ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette-lite\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-lite</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/claude-mythos-fable\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">claude-mythos-fable</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/ai\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llms\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">llms</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/geospatial\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">geospatial</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/openstreetmap\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">openstreetmap</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette</a></p>",
